    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0756" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15232</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-13">July 13, 1939</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Suma<anchor n="96" xml:id="d483-f1"/> said that the Embassy had received a
                    telegram from the Japanese Foreign Office reporting the representations made by
                    Mr. Dooman to the Japanese Foreign Minister on July 10 in regard to the recent
                    bombings of Chungking. Mr. Suma said that the report received by the Embassy
                    indicated that, even prior to the making by Mr. Dooman of representations, the
                    Japanese Foreign Office had <pb facs="0757" n="661" xml:id="pg661"/> gotten in
                    touch with the Japanese Navy Department in regard to the bombings.</p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d483-f1" n="96" xml:id="d483-f1-content">
                <p>Counselor of the Japanese Embassy.</p>
